{
  "version": 1,
  "board": "arduino:avr:uno",
  "control_period_ms": 5,
  "planning_notes": [
    "Board is authoritative: arduino:avr:uno. Wiring is preserved to D8/D9 (entrance HC-SR04), D10/D11 (exit HC-SR04), D7 (DHT11), D5 (fan PWM), D4/D3 (TM1637), and D2 (toggle button).",
    "Control period (5 ms) is scheduling granularity only; ultrasonic acquisition and validity capture are sampled at 75 ms (rounded to a multiple of the control period while meeting HC-SR04 timeout constraints).",
    "Ultrasonic invalid/out-of-range reads keep the last valid distance and set the corresponding *_valid flag false; invalid handling is done in SysML using validity.",
    "DHT temperature/humidity/validity are declared for the same physical pin D7 and sensor type DHT11; initial temperature/humidity are 0 and validity is false until first valid read (invalid_policy hold_last_valid).",
    "TM1637 number initial is 0 (default people count at startup); the D2 button semantics and display switching behavior are implemented in SysML, not by this request.",
    "Fan PWM initial is 0 so the system starts in the closed/energy-saving state until model logic opens it (thresholds and transitions belong in SysML).",
    "Serial uses baud 9600 with framing line_or_idle and idle_timeout_ms=20; exact report cadence and the business condition that drives the serial trigger are handled in SysML."
  ],
